  ### 1. Structure of the Converted .jsonl Files                                                       
                                                                                                       
  We created three distinct formats in converted so you can train with any post-training framework     
  (Axolotl, LLaMA-Factory, TRL/Hugging Face SFTTrainer, or Unsloth):                                   
  ──────                                                                                               
  #### Format A: fable5_sft_qwen_native.jsonl (Recommended for Qwen 3.8 / 2.5)                         
                                                                                                       
  This format maps directly to the official Qwen 3.8 / 2.5 chat template, which separates Chain of     
  Thought reasoning from tool invocations and text outputs.                                            
                                                                                                       
  ##### Schema Breakdown:                                                                              
                                                                                                       
    {                                                                                                  
      "id": "f956721a-0af7-4bdc-8678-3a493d8fcd39#5",                                                  
      "session": "f956721a-0af7-4bdc-8678-3a493d8fcd39",                                               
      "output_type": "tool_use",                                                                       
      "origin": "local",                                                                               
      "messages": [                                                                                    
        {                                                                                              
          "role": "system",                                                                            
          "content": "You are an expert AI coding assistant..."                                        
        },                                                                                             
        {                                                                                              
          "role": "user",                                                                              
          "content": "Make a new one, it should be a fast paced multiplayer FPS..."                    
        },                                                                                             
        {                                                                                              
          "role": "assistant",                                                                         
          "content": "",                                                                               
          "tool_calls": [                                                                              
            {                                                                                          
              "type": "function",                                                                      
              "function": {                                                                            
                "name": "Bash",                                                                        
                "arguments": {                                                                         
                  "command": "cat package.json"                                                        
                }                                                                                      
              }                                                                                        
            }                                                                                          
          ]                                                                                            
        },                                                                                             
        {                                                                                              
          "role": "tool",                                                                              
          "content": "{\"name\": \"ai-archives\", \"dependencies\": {...}}"                            
        },                                                                                             
        {                                                                                              
          "role": "assistant",                                                                         
          "reasoning_content": "Alright, I've got a decent overview of the repository...",             
          "content": "",                                                                               
          "tool_calls": [                                                                              
            {                                                                                          
              "type": "function",                                                                      
              "function": {                                                                            
                "name": "Read",                                                                        
                "arguments": {                                                                         
                  "file_path": "/home/lane/AIArchives/server/index.js"                                 
                }                                                                                      
              }                                                                                        
            }                                                                                          
          ]                                                                                            
        }                                                                                              
      ]                                                                                                
    }                                                                                                  
                                                                                                       
  ##### How Qwen's Tokenizer Renders This:                                                             
                                                                                                       
    <|im_start|>system                                                                                 
    You are an expert AI coding assistant...<|im_end|>                                                 
    <|im_start|>user                                                                                   
    Make a new one...<|im_end|>                                                                        
    <|im_start|>assistant                                                                              
    <tool_call>                                                                                        
    <function=Bash>                                                                                    
    <parameter=command>                                                                                
    cat package.json                                                                                   
    </parameter>                                                                                       
    </function>                                                                                        
    </tool_call><|im_end|>                                                                             
    <|im_start|>user                                                                                   
    <tool_response>                                                                                    
    {"name": "ai-archives", "dependencies": {...}}                                                     
    </tool_response><|im_end|>                                                                         
    <|im_start|>assistant                                                                              
    <think>                                                                                            
    Alright, I've got a decent overview of the repository...                                           
    </think>                                                                                           
                                                                                                       
    <tool_call>                                                                                        
    <function=Read>                                                                                    
    <parameter=file_path>                                                                              
    /home/lane/AIArchives/server/index.js                                                              
    </parameter>                                                                                       
    </function>                                                                                        
    </tool_call><|im_end|>                                                                             
  ──────                                                                                               
  #### Format B: fable5_sft_chatml_inline.jsonl (Standard SFT format)                                  
                                                                                                       
  In this format, the thinking trace is placed inline as <think>\n...\n</think> directly inside        
  content.                                                                                             
                                                                                                       
  ##### Schema Breakdown:                                                                              
                                                                                                       
    {                                                                                                  
      "id": "f956721a-0af7-4bdc-8678-3a493d8fcd39#5",                                                  
      "messages": [                                                                                    
        {"role": "system", "content": "You are an expert AI coding assistant..."},                     
        {"role": "user", "content": "Make a new one..."},                                              
        {                                                                                              
          "role": "assistant",                                                                         
          "content": "<think>\nAlright, I've got a decent overview...                                  
  \n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=Read>\n<parameter=file_path>\n/home/lane/AIArchives/server/index
  .js\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>"                                                        
        }                                                                                              
      ]                                                                                                
    }                                                                                                  
                                                                                                       
  Best used if your training framework does not yet support the reasoning_content dictionary key.      
  ──────                                                                                               
  #### Format C: fable5_sft_sessions.jsonl (Full Multi-Turn Sessions)                                  
                                                                                                       
  Contains 60 complete, uninterrupted developer sessions (from initial user prompt to finished         
  project). Each row contains between 15 to 400+ sequential turns of tool use, observations, reasoning,
  and code generation.                                                                                 
  ──────                                                                                               
  ### 2. How Post-Training On These Traces Teaches Fable 5 Reasoning                                   
                                                                                                       
  During SFT, the loss calculation uses Loss Masking (as implemented in validation.py:305-330):        
                                                                                                       
    [SYSTEM PROMPT]          --> Label = -100  (Masked, No Loss)                                       
    [USER QUERY]             --> Label = -100  (Masked, No Loss)                                       
    [PRIOR TOOL RESPONSES]   --> Label = -100  (Masked, No Loss)                                       
    [<think> ... </think>]   --> Label = TOKENS (SUPERVISED WITH CROSS-ENTROPY LOSS)                   
    [<tool_call> ... ]       --> Label = TOKENS (SUPERVISED WITH CROSS-ENTROPY LOSS)                   
                                                                                                       
  Because both the reasoning block (cot) and the concrete action (output) are supervised together, the 
  model learns the direct causal relationship between thinking and tool invocation:                    
                                                                                                       
    graph LR                                                                                           
        A["Observations / Terminal Output"] --> B["<think> Fable-5 Reasoning: Root Cause Analysis &    
  Planning </think>"]                                                                                  
        B --> C["Precise Tool Call (Bash, Edit, Read, Write)"]                                         
                                                                                                       
  #### What Behaviors the Model Internalizes from Fable 5:                                             
                                                                                                       
  1. Exploratory Pre-Computation:                                                                      
  Before modifying code, the model learns to think through directory structures, check package.json /  
  build scripts, and read definitions before issuing edits.                                            
  2. Observation-Driven Self-Correction:                                                               
  When a compiler error or tool failure arrives in TOOL RESULT, the model's <think> block diagnoses the
  error trace step-by-step rather than blindly repeating failed commands.                              
  3. High-Signal Tool Calling:                                                                         
  The model learns when to use Bash (compiling, grep, test runners) vs Edit (surgical line-targeted    
  edits) vs Write (fresh module creation) with valid JSON parameters.                                  
  4. Autonomous Completion Verification:                                                               
  The model learns Fable 5's pattern of running playtests, headless checks, or smoke tests to verify   
  changes before producing the final summary text.       